course: dictionary
lesson: 2937
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which one the writer means. «Dream» is a good example. Ask yourself: is this sentence about sleep, about hopes, or about thinking when you should be listening?
explain: «I had a strange dream last night about flying over the sea.» Here dream is a noun: the pictures and stories your mind makes while you sleep. Now read «My dream is to be a vet.» The clue is «my dream is to be». Nobody is asleep here. Dream means a hope or wish for the future.
explain: Dream can also be a verb, a doing word. «He dreams that his bedclothes have run downstairs» means he sees it in his sleep. Try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word. They tell you which meaning fits.
fact: «Dream» can be a noun (a dream) or a verb (to dream). The past form can be dreamed or dreamt.
fact: A dream is a set of pictures, thoughts and feelings that happen in your mind while you sleep.
fact: A dream can also be something you wish for very much, like «my dream is to be a vet».
fact: «It was all a dream» is a story ending where nothing really happened. «Dream big» means aim high.
exercise: «I had a strange dream about flying over the sea last night.» What does dream mean here? | *A set of pictures and feelings in your mind while you sleep | Thinking about other things instead of listening | Something you wish for very much | A cosy bed for sleeping in
exercise: «My dream is to be a vet.» What does dream mean here? | *A hope or wish for the future | A soft cloud | A set of pictures in your mind while you sleep | Falling asleep in class
exercise: Which word in «He dreamed of a ladder to heaven» is the verb? | ladder | He | *dreamed | heaven
test: «Ana sat at the back and let her mind dream while the teacher talked.» What does dream mean here? | Had a sleep in class | *Thought about other things instead of paying attention | Drew a map of the room | Sang a song to herself
test: «Some scientists think octopuses might have a kind of dreaming, but it is still argued.» What does «it is still argued» tell you? | It has been proved beyond doubt | *People still disagree about it | Octopuses are arguing with the scientists | It only happens at night
exam: In «His toes are freezing, and he dreams that his bedclothes have run downstairs to the kitchen fire to get warm.», which meaning fits best? | Thinking about other things instead of listening | A window that opens onto the sea | A wish for the future | *A set of pictures and stories in his mind while he sleeps
